RF.put("questb:b55",{"8695":{"id":8695,"t":"Cape of Eternal Justice","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 1 Qiraji Regal Drape, 2 Obsidian Idols, 5 Gold Scarabs and 5 Clay Scarabs to Keyl Swiftclaw in Silithus. You must also obtain Revered reputation with Cenarion Circle to complete this quest.\nQiraji Regal Drape General Rajaxx 40 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Kurinnaxx 40 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Ayamiss the Hunter 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Buru the Gorger 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj\n2 Obsidian Idol Flesh Hunter 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Drone 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Collector 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Soldier 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj and 4 more\n5 Gold Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Clay Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 21000 reputation with Cenarion Circle","desc":"I'm glad to hear you're aiding us in our attack on Ahn'Qiraj, ‹name›. I can make you a protective item that'll be of assistance in the fight against our enemy, ‹class›.\nI shall need a Qiraji drape, which I'll resize for you of course. I'll also need idols and scarabs which I'll use to create a suitable clasp.\nI promise you won't be disappointed.","rew":"You will receive:\nCape of Eternal Justice\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Did you bring the materials for the cape, ‹name›?","done":"Ah yes... this drape is immaculate.\nTake this cloak, ‹name›. May it protect you from the foul magic of the Qiraji.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":51.8,"y":39.5,"n":"Keyl Swiftclaw","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8615":{"id":8615,"t":"The Horde Needs Baked Salmon!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 1 instead of 20.","obj":"Bring 20 Baked Salmon to Chief Sharpclaw at the Valley of Spirits in Orgrimmar.\n20 Baked Salmon","desc":"The Ahn'Qiraj war effort is an immense undertaking, ‹class›. All of the materials being gathered here, whether it is metal for weapons, or food to eat, are all as important as the other. For, if you haven't eaten in days you will not have the strength to lift your axe when it matters.\nThus, we gather what food we can. I am collecting baked salmon, a dish that was chosen both for its sustenance and its ability to keep well. Can you aid me with this task, ‹class›?","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Horde Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","back":"The sprite darters can be dangerous critters when provoked. Be careful when dealing with them, ‹class›. And be even more careful of any night elves in the area. The pestering fools tend to hold up in the forests also.\nWhen you've gotten enough of the wings, let me know, I'll be sure to reward you well!","done":"Wonderful, ‹class›! These will do nicely. There are enough here to make a cloak for Korrin, and possibly even more! Thank you.\nI hope the trip wasn't too dangerous? The area of Feralas is not known for being forgiving, but you've obviously done well enough.\nThank you again, ‹class›.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":28.8,"y":68.4,"n":"Chief Sharpclaw","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"8855":{"id":8855,"t":"Thirty Signets for War Supplies","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"30 Horde Commendation Signet","rew":"You will receive:\nAhn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":29.8,"y":67.3,"n":"Warlord Gorchuk","s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"535":{"id":535,"t":"Valik","lv":34,"min":29,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a mug of Southshore Stout to Valik in the Syndicate camp.\nSouthshore Stout Drunken Footpad 99.4 % , sold by Barkeep Kelly , sold by Innkeeper Shay","desc":"Urrgh... Injured and dying and confronted with the enemy.\nNo doubt you'll kill me anyway, but if you bring me some Southshore stout--your kind does drink, don't they?--I'll tell you what you want to know.","rew":"You will receive:\nSyndicate Missive\nExperience: 270","back":"Did you bring me something to drink or did you just come back to finish the job?","done":"Given my impending death, I think I can safely say that this is the sweetest tasting thing ever... Here, take this, won't do me any good when I'm dead.\nWell, get on with it!","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":57.2,"y":69.5,"n":"Henchman Valik","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["alterac-mountains"]},"8375":{"id":8375,"t":"Remember Alterac Valley!","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 8,300 experience instead of 11,900, 0.7 times as much.","obj":"Bring 3 Alterac Valley Marks of Honor to an Alliance Brigadier General outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Alterac Valley Mark of Honor","desc":"Make no mistake about it, ‹name›. The Horde is quite right when they say Alterac Valley is Frostwolf Territory.\nYou see, the Stormpike Expedition arrived as peaceful visitors to the area in search of ore and relics. The Frostwolves reacted with the most brutal and uncivilized act of aggression the Alliance has experienced.\nLet us never forget the brave dwarves that perished in that cowardly unannounced attack. Go now, ‹class›, do your part in the battle for Alterac Valley. For the Alliance!","rew":"Money: 1 80 1 gold, 80 silver, 0 copper Experience: 8,300\n+150 reputation with Stormpike Guard","back":"What news do you bring from the lands of the Stormpikes? How does the battle for Alterac Valley fare?","done":"You've shown great bravery in protecting our lands in Alterac Valley! I will tell my superiors of your deeds.\nDun Morogh Darnassus Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.3,"y":35.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":58,"y":34.2,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":81.2,"y":38.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["alterac-mountains"]},"695":{"id":695,"t":"An Apprentice's Enchantment","lv":39,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Skuerto.\nProvided: Enchanted Agate","desc":"Here you are, ‹name›. The gem only needs to be pressed against one of the pedestals near the base of the tower to activate its defenses. Use it when you're ready to enter the tower and find Trelane's remaining items.\nGood luck to you. I'll be awaiting your return here at the camp. Oh, and speak to Skuerto before you leave. He'll give you the rest of the details you'll need.","rew":"Experience: 300\n+25 reputation with Ironforge","done":"Good, good.\nIf there are no other delays, how about we get started?","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":46.2,"y":47.8,"n":"Apprentice Kryten","s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":46.7,"y":47,"n":"Skuerto","e":1}],"cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"4295":{"id":4295,"t":"Rocknot's Ale","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"2 Dark Iron Ale Mug Whit Wantmal , Dark Iron Ale Mug , Grim Guzzler Boar 4.1 % , Guzzling Patron 0.6 % and 4 more","back":"Oh, ale! I would kill for some Dark Iron ale!! Quick, I'm getting sober! I know this because sobriety blurs my vision... and it's making you look like the ‹race› I slew last week!","done":"What's this? Ah! It smells like Dark Iron Ale! Drink has blurred my sight, but I can tell that you, sir, are a real friend!\nStart Private Rocknot End Private Rocknot Level 1 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 4 6 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Dungeon Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 4295","cats":["blackrock-depths"]},"9015":{"id":9015,"t":"The Challenge","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to the Ring of the Law in Blackrock Depths and place the Banner of Provocation in its center as you are sentenced by High Justice Grimstone. Slay Theldren and his gladiators and return to Anthion Harmon in the Eastern Plaguelands with the first piece of Lord Valthalak's amulet.\nTop Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet Theldren\nProvided: Banner of Provocation","desc":"Heed me well, ‹name›. For the banner to work in the desired way, you will need to step into the Ring of the Law in Blackrock Depths. Allow yourself to be sentenced by High Justice Grimstone and place the banner firmly on the ground in a sign of defiance.\nYour victim will not be able to restrain himself and shall enter the fray filled with a desire to fight you. Once you obtain that which you seek, go back to Anthion.","rew":"Experience: 6,600","back":"You're back, ‹name›!","done":"You've recovered part of the medallion, ‹name›?","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":26.1,"y":11.3,"n":"Anthion Harmon","e":1}],"cats":["blackrock-depths"]},"7655":{"id":7655,"t":"Imperial Plate Bracer","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"20 Thorium Bar","rew":"You will receive:\nPlans: Imperial Plate Bracers\n+100 reputation with Thorium Brotherhood","back":"For the bracer plans, I'll be needin' 20 thorium bars.\nAre you alright, sonny? Yer getting' all red.","done":"A pleasure doin' business with ya.\nAnd ‹name›, wipe that look of disgust off yer face.","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":51.4,"y":28.7,"n":"Derotain Mudsipper","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blacksmithing"]},"96055":{"id":96055,"t":"Camping 101 herbalism","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Reyna Stonebranch in Ironforge to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your herbalism skill to 20","desc":"Looks to me like you've gained some skill in herbalism. Picking flowers isn't just for dilly-dallying, you know. It can be useful... and profitable.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Incense Candle for your camp. High spirits are a key component to keeping healers and spellcasters in the fight, and an Incense Candle can provide a boost that magic users will surely appreciate.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Incense Candle. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.\nDun Morogh Ironforge","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":46.6,"y":53.8,"n":"Eric Brighthammer","s":1},{"z":"Ironforge","x":55.6,"y":58.8,"n":"Reyna Stonebranch","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94215":{"id":94215,"t":"Craftsmans writ free action potion","min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet. Partly read from what players of our addon saw in game.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Free Action Potion\nFree Action Potion","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting 1 Free Action Potion, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin Pouch\n+75 reputation with Azeroth Commerce Authority\n+75 reputation with Durotar Supply and Logistics","back":"<You approach a thrashing creature clearly trapped in spider silk, at the precise location the writ indicated.>","done":"<You waste little time offering the wiggling mass the Free Action Potion that was requested. It seems either unaware of your presence, or unable to claim the item.\nA handful of coins are scattered just beside the cocoon. You may decide to leave the potion there, and take the coins for yourself. Nature will surely sort itself out, in that case.>","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":62.5,"y":69.3,"n":"Webbed Mudsnout Gnoll","e":1}],"cats":["crafting"]},"94295":{"id":94295,"t":"Craftsmans writ wild leather helmet","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Wild Leather Helmet\nWild Leather Helmet","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Wild Leather Helmet, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Wild Leather Helmet Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94295","cats":["crafting"]},"7895":{"id":7895,"t":"Whirring Bronze Gizmo","lv":60,"min":10,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"7 Whirring Bronze Gizmo Narillasanz 0.3 % , Stonevault Brawler 0 % , Daggerspine Raider 0 % , Scarlet Paladin 0 % and 1 more","rew":"You will receive:\n4 Darkmoon Faire Prize Ticket\n+100 reputation with Darkmoon Faire","back":"My new booth will be a sight to see, yes sir! A sight to see, and... for a lucky few, to touch!\nI can already hear the whirring bronze gizmos singing their song of mechanical rapture as patrons step to my booth and test their skill!\nAh... now I need the gizmos themselves to bring my dream closer to fruition. Please, ‹name›, bring me whirring bronze gizmos... and Darkmoon Faire tickets will be yours!","done":"You brought the gizmos! Wonderful! Even now I can hear their buzzing, whirring chorus in my mind! Oh, when this booth is ready it will be the wonder of the world, mark me!\nHere are your tickets, ‹name›. And please enjoy your stay at the Faire!\nMulgore Elwynn Forest","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":38,"y":44.3,"n":"Rinling","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":41.7,"y":70.7,"n":"Rinling","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkmoon-faire"]},"55":{"id":55,"t":"Morbent Fel","lv":32,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use Morbent's Bane on Morbent Fel, kill Morbent Fel, then return Morbent's Bane to Sven at his camp.\nMorbent's Bane\nMorbent Fel slain\nProvided: Morbent's Bane","desc":"Morbent Fel hides in his lair, the house perched atop the hill to the east overlooking the Raven Hill cemetery. His time in this land is drawing to an end...\nUse Morbent's Bane against him. It will render his protective magics powerless.\nSlay him. Slay him, and save us from his wickedness. Be the instrument of my revenge, and a hero of Duskwood!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nNight Watch Pantaloons Watch Master's Cloak Sparkmetal Coif\nYou will also receive:\nTorch of Holy Flame\nExperience: 3,850\n+200 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Is Morbent Fel defeated?!","done":"Morbent Fel has been defeated. The dark riders are still at large, but a small piece of that which I had hoped beyond hope has come to pass.\nYou have done the impossible, and your deeds will forever live in the legends of Duskwood.\nGo, ‹name›. And perhaps, one day, fate may bring you back to me...","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":7.8,"y":34.1,"n":"Sven Yorgen","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"6135":{"id":6135,"t":"Duskwing, Oh How I Hate Thee...","lv":60,"min":56,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Duskwing and slay him. From the corpse, recover a Patch of Duskwing's Fur and return it to Nathanos Blightcaller.\nIt is said that Duskwing roams the countryside to the north of Marris Stead.\nPatch of Duskwing's Fur Duskwing","desc":"Up until now, you have completed the missions I have assigned; even if not in the most timely manner.\nI suppose you think that you are ready for a challenge. Yes... Yes, imbecile, perhaps you are ready for a more involved set of missions.\nThe albino demon bat, Duskwing, roams the countryside just north of here. Track him down and destroy him. Return to me with a patch of his white fur and you shall be rewarded.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nDuskwing Gloves Duskwing Mantle\nMoney: 90 0 gold, 90 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"I would not recommend that you take on this challenge alone, ‹class›.","done":"Excellent work, imbecile. I shall fashion this fur into something you can use.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":22.2,"y":63.5,"n":"Nathanos Blightcaller","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"4135":{"id":4135,"t":"The Writhing Deep","lv":46,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Now that Raschal's last known whereabouts have been discovered, continue your search for him or his remains in the Writhing Deep. According to the note, it is located to the south of the Woodpaw gnoll camps.\nProvided: Undelivered Parcel","desc":"Inside the backpacks are two items: the first is a parcel of goods that was bound for Thalanaar, and the second is a note hastily penned to an unknown reader.\nThe note tells of discovering insidious bug-like creatures south of the gnoll camps in a place called the Writhing Deep. The author felt the need to investigate it personally, as though it was a serious threat to all of Feralas. The note is signed, \"Raschal of Feathermoon\".\nIt would seem that you have located where Raschal ultimately went.","rew":"Experience: 3,050\n+75 reputation with Darnassus","done":"You have discovered a large pod of an alien nature. The texture of the pod appears mucous, though hardened protrusions stick out from random parts of it. The pod itself has the height and width to easily encompass a humanoid inside of it... and from the faint humanoid shape visible through the skin of the pod, you surmise that this is what it indeed encapsulates.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":73.3,"y":56.3,"n":"Large Leather Backpacks","s":1},{"z":"Feralas","x":72.1,"y":63.7,"n":"Zukk'ash Pod","e":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"7735":{"id":7735,"t":"Pristine Yeti Hide","lv":48,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Pristine Yeti Hide to Pratt McGrubben at the Feathermoon Stronghold, Feralas.\nPristine Yeti Hide Lurking Feral Scar 25 % , Ferocious Rage Scar 10 % , Elder Rage Scar 10 % , Rage Scar Yeti 10 %\nProvided: Pristine Yeti Hide","desc":"You have found a pristine yeti hide that is exceptionally thick and sturdy - more so than even the ones you've seen from the yeti in Rage Scar.\nConsidering that Pratt McGrubben at the Feathermoon Stronghold is in the market for yeti hides, this particular one may be of considerable interest to him.","rew":"Money: 70 0 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,200\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"What's this, ‹name› - you've got something special for me?","done":"Incredible! You may have found the granddaddy of all yeti hides with this!\nYou better believe I'll pay you for it. I normally don't pay that much for a single hide, but I'm pretty sure I can make something special from it. Thanks for thinking of me on this, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":30.6,"y":42.7,"n":"Pratt McGrubben","e":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"9335":{"id":9335,"t":"Consecrated Sharpening Stones","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Level 60 instead of 0.","obj":"8 Necrotic Rune Bone Witch , Spirit of the Damned , Lumbering Horror , Shadow of Doom 38.4 % and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\nConsecrated Sharpening Stone","back":"If you bring me eight necrotic runes from the Scourge invaders, I can give you a consecrated sharpening stone. It should be of great help in your battle against the minions of the Lich King.","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Here are your consecrated sharpening stones. Use them prudently.\nUndercity Orgrimmar Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":65,"y":45.6,"n":"Argent Outfitter","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":52.2,"y":73.8,"n":"Argent Outfitter","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":42.1,"y":58.5,"n":"Argent Outfitter","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["invasion"]},"8935":{"id":8935,"t":"Just Compensation","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a Shadowcraft Belt and a set of Shadowcraft Gloves to Deliana in Ironforge.\nShadowcraft Belt Blackhand Assassin 7 % , Smolderthorn Shadow Hunter 3.1 % , Bloodaxe Warmonger 2.1 % , Firebrand Legionnaire 2.1 % and 3 more\nShadowcraft Gloves Shadow Hunter Vosh'gajin 0 %","desc":"You kept your word and brought the device built by Mux. I believe a reward is in order if I'm to keep you interested in saving my skin. Bring me the belt and set of gloves that you wish to upgrade. I promise the ones I give you in return will be far superior.","rew":"You will receive:\nDarkmantle Belt Darkmantle Gloves\nExperience: 9,950","back":"You're ready to perform the trade?","done":"You've kept your end of the bargain, I shall keep mine.\nJust remember that I'm holding on to the best pieces until your work is finished.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58.1,"y":29.5,"n":"Deliana","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"2855":{"id":2855,"t":"Wild Leather Shoulders","lv":45,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 6 Thick Armor Kits and a Wildvine to Jangdor Swiftstrider in Camp Mojache.\n6 Thick Armor Kit Olaf 0 %\nWildvine Retherokk the Berserker 80.6 % , Zul'arek Hatefowler 65.1 % , Purple Lotus 10 % , Vilebranch Aman'zasi Guard 9.5 % and 4 more","desc":"Wild Leather shoulders support a wearer's frame extremely well, offering superior protection of the upper arms as well as the shoulders. As with all Wild Leather armor, a random yet very potent enhancement is imbued within the item as the wildvine is stitched in.\nFor this pattern, I will require six thick armor kits and a wildvine. That shouldn't be too tall of an order for you to fill.","rew":"You will receive:\nPattern: Wild Leather Shoulders\nExperience: 2,900","back":"Do you have the six thick armor kits and the wildvine I require?\nThink of making armor kits as a lesson in steady and reliable crafting; the consistent fashioning method you develop as you ply your trade on these kits helps develop your skills for the intricate work needed to make Wild Leather armors.\nEvery lesson has a purpose, ‹name›. It is important to embrace each one accordingly.","done":"These armor kits are of solid quality, ‹name›. If there is one thing I demand in not only my work, but in the work of those I give tutelage to, it is quality.\nYou've done well to earn this pattern; I hope it brings you the rewards it has brought me.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":74.4,"y":42.9,"n":"Jangdor Swiftstrider","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["leatherworking"]},"79975":{"id":79975,"t":"Eagles fist","lv":32,"min":14,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Water spray dampens the air, the view is incredible.","desc":"<You find a carefully folded letter inside of the toolbox.>\n\"From here, with the right tools, you call the shots. Great place to launch a parachute glider.\nMy loyalty to the Eagle and Fist requires distance in order to serve them best. This barricade has had better days, like the Old Kingdoms it once defended, but I'll never abandon it.\"","done":"A campfire is newly fed with wood, but signs of a quick departure are evident.\nLoch Modan Arathi Highlands","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":49.5,"y":12.8,"n":"Carved Figurine","s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":22.5,"y":24.2,"n":"Messenger Bag","e":1}],"cats":["loch-modan"]},"775":{"id":775,"t":"Journey into Thunder Bluff","lv":10,"min":3,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Cairne Bloodhoof in Thunder Bluff.","desc":"You will now be revered within our great city. Any ‹race› worthy of completing the Rites of the Earthmother earns that honor.\nFor your final quest, seek out our noble leader, Cairne Bloodhoof, who dwells atop the highest mesa in Thunder Bluff.","rew":"Experience: 420\n+50 reputation with Thunder Bluff","done":"Hail, young ‹class›. I see you found your way to my doorstep.\nMulgore Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":58.3,"y":30.7,"n":"Ancestral Spirit","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":60.3,"y":51.7,"n":"Cairne Bloodhoof","e":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"9095":{"id":9095,"t":"Frostfire Robe","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Archmage Angela Dosantos at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make a Frostfire Robe if you bring her the following: 1 Desecrated Robe, 25 Wartorn Cloth Scraps, 4 Mooncloth and 2 Nexus Crystals.\nDesecrated Robe\n25 Wartorn Cloth Scrap Stoneskin Gargoyle 35 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 30.3 % in Naxxramas , Bile Retcher 28.5 % in Naxxramas , Mad Scientist 28.3 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n4 Mooncloth\n2 Nexus Crystal","desc":"As a Watcher, I was allowed access to many of Medivh's personal effects. Among those items, I found the tomes most enlightening. While the majority of the books were filled with - to put it bluntly - tripe, there were some gems. One of those tomes documented the creation of a set of armor fit for an archmage: Frostfire.\n<Angela points to her head.>\nIt's all in here and I am willing to share the fruits of that knowledge with you as long as you are able to provide me with the necessary materials.","rew":"You will receive:\nFrostfire Robe\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"ou got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !,\nyou got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Frostfire Robe.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":48.7,"n":"Archmage Angela Dosantos","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"1655":{"id":1655,"t":"Bailor's Ore Shipment","lv":22,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Jordan's Ore Shipment to Bailor Stonehand in Loch Modan.\nJordan's Ore Shipment Mo'grosh Mystic , Mo'grosh Shaman , Mo'grosh Enforcer , Mo'grosh Ogre and 1 more","desc":"Ach, ya startled me, man/woman! Can't ya see I was lost in thought?\nWhat's that? Jordan's shipment... fer Ironforge. Ahhh, yeah, I know whatcha speak of. Mo'grosh ogres... dat's who took me ol' friend's ore shipment. Caravan was headin' here from the Wetlands and was ambushed. The guard who survived their attack just passed away a few days ago--healer couldn't get to 'em fast enough.\nIf you want the shipment, you'll have to head northeast across the Loch. It's got to be there somewhere.","rew":"You will receive:\nJordan's Refined Ore Shipment\nExperience: 440","back":"So, any luck yet? Haha, those ogres didn't get the best of ya yet, did they?","done":"Yup yup, this is it. Ha! If I'd known you were really gonna head out there and fight some o' them ogres, I woulda given you a list of things to get instead of just this one thing. But, you're not here doin' business for me, are ya?.\nA deal's a deal; Jordan wanted a shipment of me alloy, that's what he's gonna get.\nTell 'em hello fer me, and be safe, ‹class›.","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":36,"y":44.9,"n":"Bailor Stonehand","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"94775":{"id":94775,"t":"Divine grace","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak to High Priestess Laurena in Stormwind.","desc":"Elune bless you, good ‹race›. I hope your Light finds you and protects you well this day.\nOne of your priests was here not long ago looking for you. He mentioned you returning to the Cathedral of Light as soon as possible to speak with High Priestess Laurena. It seems you've done well to garner such attention. I wouldn't spend too much time here--your people have need of you.\nLevel 10 , requires level 10 Difficulty 10 13 16 Side Alliance Class Priest Shareable Yes Quest ID 94775","cats":["priest"]},"5655":{"id":5655,"t":"Hex of Weakness","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Ur'kyo in Orgrimmar.","desc":"I sent here to make sure that you not wander too far from home, ‹name›. They send me to make sure you return home because Ur'kyo, greatest of our priests, wish to speak to you. You go there. You go to the Valley of Spirits in the orc city and you speak to Ur'kyo. He wait for you now.","rew":"You will learn: Hex of Weakness\nExperience: 210","done":"You would do well to pay heed to this lesson, young one. The Hex of Weakness will be a great boon to you in battle. Later I will have tests for you to further yourself and prove your worth to the tribe.\nDurotar Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":54.3,"y":42.9,"n":"Tai'jin","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":35.6,"y":87.8,"n":"Ur'kyo","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"94375":{"id":94375,"t":"Call of earth","lv":4,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the Rough Quartz to Teo Hammerstorm in Anvilmar.\nProvided: Rough Quartz","desc":"Take this rough quartz from me and bring it to Teo Hammerstorm as proof o' our meeting. He will craft a totem for ye, and this pebble will be the heart o' it. As small as it may seem, ye will come to find that size does not matter, and that even the smallest o' things can outlast many others.\nBe patient, ‹name›. Remain strong. And seek wisdom. This is what earth asks o' ye. In the end, ye shall become one with the earth--respect it as it shall respect ye.","rew":"You will receive:\nEarth Totem\nExperience: 450","back":"Ahh, ye've returned. If ye have the stone, it means the mountain's chosen ye true. I'll give ye the totem it promised. But if ye've come empty-handed, off with ye! The path ain't for those who forget their way.","done":"Well done! Know this - totems ain't just a mark of yer place among shamans. They're tools, a focus for spells tied to stone, soil, and other elements. As ye grow wiser, more o' the mountain's power will open to ye. The trainers will know when yer ready for more. But for now, take this totem, and let the ground speak through ye.\nDurotar Mulgore Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":44,"y":76,"n":"Minor Manifestation of Earth","s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":53.8,"y":80.4,"n":"Minor Manifestation of Earth","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":28.7,"y":66.1,"n":"Teo Hammerstorm","e":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"96135":{"id":96135,"t":"Heed my call","lv":40,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Use the Twisted Totems to put an end to the quilboar ritual.\nEye of the Tempest\nProvided: Corrupted Totems","desc":"Euck, just bein' around these blasted totems is givin' me the willies--but that's good. This much twisted corruption will be exactly what we need tae summon the quilboar's elementals.\nGo to the Thousand Needles and find a suitable spot for your defenses. The steam pools should work. They're rich with fire, earth, water, and air alike. Place these totems and be ready for a fight. The Razormane won't take too kindly to yer interference.","rew":"Money: 50 0 gold, 50 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,150\nArathi Highlands Thousand Needles","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":59.8,"y":27.6,"n":"Veyric Thunderhame","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"8535":{"id":8535,"t":"Hoary Templar","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Summon and slay a Hoary Templar and report back to Bor Wildmane in Cenarion Hold. You must also bring Tactical Task Briefing IV in order to complete this quest.\nTactical Task Briefing IV\nHoary Templar slain\nProvided: Tactical Task Briefing IV","desc":"The Twilight's Hammer and the elemental nobles they worship present a formidable threat to our operations in Silithus. With the new enemies we're facing inside Ahn'Qiraj, we cannot afford to lower our guard to our enemies outside.\nFind a way to summon and destroy a Hoary Templar and report to Bor Wildmane.","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Tactical Badge Tactical Assignment\nExperience: 650\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Is your task done yet, ‹name›?","done":"Good job, ‹name›. Here's your next assignment.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":48.6,"y":37.8,"n":"Bor Wildmane","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"9415":{"id":9415,"t":"Report to Marshal Bluewall","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 1 instead of 53.","obj":"Speak with Marshal Bluewall at the Alliance encampment near Hive'Zora.","desc":"Are you Marshal Bluewall's new recruits? Of course you are.\nWhat are you waiting for? Good soldiers are dying in the desert. Aren't you excited to join them?\nNow, get going and don't dry out on the way.","done":"The Alliance needs every able body they can get. The Horde has been receiving a steady supply of reinforcements from the northern part of the continent, and it's been a struggle to keep up.\nLet me explain the situation to you.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":50.7,"y":34.7,"n":"Rifleman Torrig","s":1},{"z":"Silithus","x":33.3,"y":51.1,"n":"Marshal Bluewall","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"8775":{"id":8775,"t":"Target: Hive'Regal Spitfires","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 30 Hive'Regal Spitfires and report back to Commander Mar'alith at Cenarion Hold in Silithus. You must also bring Combat Task Briefing IX in order to complete this quest.\nCombat Task Briefing IX\nHive'Regal Spitfire slain : 0/ 30\nProvided: Combat Task Briefing IX","desc":"As the war effort mounts, the silithid presence in the area presents an ever increasing threat to our operations. You've been selected to partake on an assault on Hive'Regal where your primary target will consist of the airborne Hive'Regal spitfires.\nReport back to Commander Mar'alith after your task is completed.","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Combat Badge\nExperience: 650\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"You wish to tell me something, ‹name›?","done":"Excellent work, ‹name›. Your part in the attack on Hive'Regal has been noted.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":49.2,"y":34.2,"n":"Commander Mar'alith","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"79095":{"id":79095,"t":"The apothecarys metaphysical primer","lv":20,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"The Apothecary's Metaphysical Primer","rew":"You will receive:\nItem 211779\nMoney: 1 25 0 gold, 1 silver, 25 copper Experience: 160","back":"Have you brought something to add to our collection?\nThe Apothecary's Metaphysical Primer (1)","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Our knowledge expands through your efforts.\nIf you discover more magical works that might benefit the library, please bring them to me.","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":73.6,"y":33,"n":"Owen Thadd","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["special"]},"1095":{"id":1095,"t":"Further Instructions","lv":27,"min":16,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the new orders to Ziz Fizziks in the Stonetalon Mountains.","desc":"The matter of this gnome that has been hired by the Venture Company has caused a bit of a stir in Undermine. The trade princes do not approve of Razdunk's consorting with this Gerenzo.\nRiddlevox has asked me to take care of the problem, and I'm sure he was instructed to do so by one or more of the trade princes. Of course, the Director didn't tell me that. Let's just say I have a hunch.\nWhatever the case, Gerenzo must be removed, and it would be a fitting test to have Fizziks take care of him.","rew":"Experience: 1,100\n+50 reputation with Ratchet","done":"Eliminate Gerenzo? Now there is a prospect that I have no objections to.\nGnomes are bad enough as it is, but what I learned about Gerenzo only makes it worse. Apparently, he was one of the head engineers in Gnomeregan, where he was working on their secret project--we could never infiltrate Dun Morogh well enough to find out specific details. It was a failure. Our reports say that whatever it was literally exploded in their faces.\nThe Barrens Stonetalon Mountains","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":63,"y":37.2,"n":"Sputtervalve","s":1},{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":59,"y":62.6,"n":"Ziz Fizziks","e":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"1015":{"id":1015,"t":"The New Frontier","lv":55,"min":54,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm at the Cenarion Enclave of Darnassus about the Cenarion Circle's call to explore the frontiers of Kalimdor.","desc":"Attention, heroes!\nThe Cenarion Circle seeks able bodied individuals to assist them in exploring the vast new frontiers of Kalimdor! A forbidden wasteland of unimaginable dangers lies far to the west of Tanaris and Gadgetzan, and the Circle needs willing and honorable proxies to act in their stead.\nAll interested individuals should seek audience with the Cenarion Circle. Speak with the Arch Druid in Darnassus, Fandral Staghelm, for more information!","rew":"Experience: 550","done":"What makes you think I wish to be pestered by the likes of you, ‹class›? Wait - let me stop the important duties I attend to on a daily basis so I can help you locate a doodad somewhere. By all means, the welfare of Darnassus - nay, all of Teldrassil - should come second to the acquisition of a bauble for your collection.\nThe fools in Moonglade waste my time with their call for assistance, and now I must endure this?\nStormwind City Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":56.4,"y":74.1,"n":"Crier Goodman","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":34.8,"y":9.3,"n":"Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"7495":{"id":7495,"t":"Victory for the Alliance","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 60 instead of 50.","obj":"Take the Head of Onyxia to Highlord Bolvar Fordragon in Stormwind.\nHead of Onyxia Onyxia\nProvided: Head of Onyxia","desc":"You have accomplished the impossible. The brood mother of the Black Dragonflight lies dead at your feet. Take her head and present it to the Highlord.","rew":"Experience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Stormwind","back":"By Uther's beard!","done":"For so many years I was held under her captivating gaze. Finally, to see justice meted and the honor of Stormwind restored! Today, we celebrate this glorious victory!","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":80.2,"y":38.3,"n":"Highlord Bolvar Fordragon","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"215":{"id":215,"t":"Jungle Secrets","lv":33,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Lieutenant Doren at the Rebel Camp.","desc":"Thank you for saving me, ‹name›. I know how this looks, but...allow me to explain.\nI was charged by Lieutenant Doren to re-enlist with Kurzen's men, so that I might spy on them and bring sorely needed intelligence to the rebels. You saw here what I had thought would be my chance to infiltrate Kurzen's Compound. I was wrong, and again, thanks for saving me.\nThis was a top secret mission, so you must tell no one. But if you speak with Doren he will explain.","rew":"Experience: 1,300\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","done":"Yes, what Thorsen told you is true. You must be discrete with this. At one time, we rebels were fiercely loyal to Colonel Kurzen. But such was Kurzen's corruption, our passion twisted into rage. If it was made known that Private Thorsen has had recent dealings with Kurzen's men, then one night he would find himself with a slit throat.\nTo my knowledge, only Sergeant Yohwa, Thorsen and I were privy to Thorsen's mission. But there must be another. A traitor.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":38,"y":3.4,"n":"Private Thorsen","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":38,"y":3,"n":"Lieutenant Doren","e":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"615":{"id":615,"t":"The Captain's Cutlass","lv":50,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Level 50 instead of 51. Gives 470 experience instead of 475, 0.99 times as much.","obj":"Speak with Sprogger.","desc":"After I lost my first ship to those giants, I bought another. Named Smotts' Revenge, I filled it with supplies and crew, and set out to find the villains. I found them, but...they beat me. They smashed Smotts' Revenge, killed my second crew and set me on another lifeboat.\nThis time another of the giants, Negolash, stole my cutlass.\nFace Negolash and bring me my cutlass!\nSpeak with Sprogger. He was my cook on the Smotts' Revenge, and survived the last attack. He can help you find the giant.","rew":"Experience: 470","done":"Hello hello, ‹name›. Captain told me you're going after Negolash, eh?\nLevel 50 , requires level 35 Difficulty 35 46 48 53 60 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Shareable Yes Quest ID 615\nThe chain\n5 quests from level 50 to 52, 17,020 XP in all.\n1 [ 50 ] The Monogrammed Sash\nReturn the Monogrammed Sash to its owner.\nMonogrammed Sash\n2,350 XP\n2 [ 50 ] The Captain's Cutlass this quest\nSpeak with Sprogger.\n470 XP\n3 [ 50 ] Facing Negolash\nBring 10 Barbecued Buzzard Wings and 5 bottles of Junglevine Wine to Captain Smotts' Lifeboat. Kill Negolash, and bring Smotts' Cutlass to Captain Smotts in Stranglethorn.\n7,100 XP\n[ 50 ] Facing Negolash\nBring 10 Barbecued Buzzard Wings and 5 bottles of Junglevine Wine to Captain Smotts' Lifeboat. Kill Negolash, and bring Smotts' Cutlass to Captain Smotts in Stranglethorn.\nSprogger Stranglethorn Vale\n7,100 XP\n4 [ 52 ] Enticing Negolash\nRuined Lifeboat Stranglethorn Vale","cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"8055":{"id":8055,"t":"Paragons of Power: The Freethinker's Breastplate","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Level 60 instead of 61. Requires level 58 instead of 60. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 6,500, 1.02 times as much.","obj":"Bring Jin'rokh the Breaker a Primal Hakkari Tabard. You must also have a reputation equal to or greater than Revered with the Zandalar Tribe.\nJin'rokh the Breaker is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale.\nPrimal Hakkari Tabard\nReach 21000 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","desc":"Battle gear gives you power in the tribe. The freethinkers are honored in this way. They are zealots. They imbue their breastplates with powerful mojo. If their beliefs falter in the face of the enemy, their breastplate will not.\nYou must be revered amongst us to possess such a breastplate. Go to Zul'Gurub. Take the Paragons of Power I need. Take the Paragons most painfully from the fools inside. Bring them to me. Prove your worth as a freethinker once and for all.","rew":"You will receive:\nZandalar Freethinker's Breastplate\nExperience: 6,600\n+150 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"Do you have the Paragons? They have mojo inside them. We must have them. You will aid us.","done":"You have done what few ever could. You have brought the minions of Hakkar to their knees. You have shown them what a freethinker can do. You have shown us how a heretic could be revered in the tribe. You have more than real power. You ARE real power.\nTake the breastplate, freethinker. Crush those who oppose you.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.3,"y":14.4,"n":"Jin'rokh the Breaker","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"935":{"id":935,"t":"Crown of the Earth","lv":11,"min":3,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Filled Vessel to Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm in Darnassus.\nFilled Vessel\nProvided: Filled Vessel","desc":"Without the blessings of Alexstrasza the Life-Binder and Nozdormu the Timeless, Teldrassil's growth has not been without flaw. Strange beasts have been reported arising from the very ground of the tree, and crazed furbolgs attack passing travelers.\nI can only hope that the solution the Arch Druid is looking for will be found quickly. I will pour all the phials you brought into this vessel, for you to deliver to Darnassus.\nBring it to Fandral Staghelm, you will find him in the druid grove.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nAshwood Bow Thicket Hammer\nExperience: 1,100\n+150 reputation with Darnassus","back":"I know that I did not summon you, so I cannot help but wonder why it is you have come to speak with me.\nWhatever it is, please make it quick.","done":"Ah yes, the water I had requested. Tenaron and Corithras certainly took their time in having it delivered... perhaps not choosing the most reliable of messengers... hmm.\nNonetheless, I can finally get back to my work then. The weight of Teldrassil's problems fall upon my shoulders. A yoke I would wish to soon be rid of.\nTake this, you may find some use for it.\nTeldrassil Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":56.1,"y":61.7,"n":"Corithras Moonrage","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":34.8,"y":9.3,"n":"Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm","e":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"855":{"id":855,"t":"Centaur Bracers","lv":14,"min":9,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 15 Centaur Bracers to Regthar Deathgate, west of the Crossroads.\n15 Centaur Bracers Verog the Dervish , Kolkar Invader 80 % , Kolkar Stormseer 80 % , Warlord Krom'zar 80 % and 4 more","desc":"The Kolkar are a threat to the Horde's claims in the Barrens; we must reduce the numbers of their troops. And so, I have a bounty task for you.\nWhile in Kolkar territories, slay their warriors and collect centaur bracers. Return when you have a heap of bracers and the Horde will reward you well.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nOrcish Battle Bow Pointed Axe Stonewood Hammer\nExperience: 1,250\n+150 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"How goes your hunting, ‹name›?","done":"Nicely done. I'm sure you've struck fear into the surviving centaurs, ‹name›. If they have sense, they'll now calm themselves and stop their advances.\nBut I don't think they will, and that is unfortunate.\nUnfortunate...for them.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":45.3,"y":28.4,"n":"Regthar Deathgate","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"95495":{"id":95495,"t":"The hermit tanner","lv":18,"min":14,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the Bundle of Hides to the hermit on the ridge overlooking the Dry Hills in the Barrens.\nProvided: Bundle of Hides","desc":"These hides are bound for a tanner who I often trade with. He is something of a hermit and he lives alone on the top of the ridge behind me. Climbing up a steep hillside isn't something I can manage easily right now so I'd be in your debt if you could make this delivery for me.\nOh, and about this tanner's... appearance. You need not be alarmed. In spite of his looks, he is no threat. I swear this is true.","back":"Greetings, ‹class›. What brings you up to my property today?","done":"Vrang sent you then? Very well. I appreciate you delivering these hides to me. It's unfortunate that Vrang couldn't make the journey himself. There is a matter I wish to speak with him about.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":43.8,"y":12.2,"n":"Vrang Wildgore","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":42,"y":11.4,"n":"Walton","e":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"2935":{"id":2935,"t":"Consult Master Gadrin","lv":45,"min":40,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Master Gadrin in Sen'jin Village.","desc":"The venom from the broodguards wasn't as potent as the venom you brought originally. It must have come from a different spider.\nI want a fresh sample of that venom. To find out where it came from, you must consult with a troll who knows the Witherbark well--Master Gadrin in Sen'jin Village. Travel to Durotar and speak with Gadrin. With luck, he'll know where the Witherbarks get their venom.","rew":"Experience: 2,900\n+75 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","done":"Ah, so you want fresh venom from the spider of the witherbarks, yes? Well, sit down... you're not going to like what I have to tell you.\nHillsbrad Foothills Durotar","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":61.4,"y":19.1,"n":"Apothecary Lydon","s":1},{"z":"Durotar","x":55.9,"y":74.7,"n":"Master Gadrin","e":1}],"cats":["the-hinterlands"]},"7815":{"id":7815,"t":"Snapjaws, Mon!","lv":50,"min":44,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Katoom the Angler at Revantusk Village in the Hinterlands wants you to kill 15 Saltwater Snapjaw turtles. Return to him when you have completed this task.\nSaltwater Snapjaw slain : 0/ 15","desc":"Don't let their big eyes fool you, mon! Those saltwater snapjaws be a menace. I can't fish for five minutes without getting a broken line from one of those oversized fish vacuums stealing my bait.\nDo me and the people of Revantusk Village a service and kill em, mon.\nKill the whole lot of em!","rew":"You will receive:\nNat Pagle's Extreme Angler FC-5000\nMoney: 75 0 gold, 75 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,700\n+100 reputation with Revantusk Trolls","back":"How goes the hunt?","done":"Oh, mon! I can't thank you enough! Hopefully this here fishing pole will be reward enough for the job.","pins":[{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":80.3,"y":81.5,"n":"Katoom the Angler","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-hinterlands"]},"1175":{"id":1175,"t":"A Bump in the Road","lv":33,"min":28,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 10 Saltstone Basilisks, 10 Saltstone Crystalhides and 6 Saltstone Gazers for Trackmaster Zherin on the Shimmering Flats.\nSaltstone Basilisk slain : 0/ 10\nSaltstone Crystalhide slain : 0/ 10\nSaltstone Gazer slain : 0/ 6","desc":"After the big crash with the goblins' Red Thunder racer and a basilisk, Kronkrider hired me on to take care of the track. I don't know what all the animals out on the flats are feeding on to grow so big, but we have to be careful to thin them out so they won't wander onto the track when a race is going on.\nTell you what. If you want to go out and make a little profit, go out and remove the basilisks from the area.","rew":"Money: 35 0 gold, 35 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,650","back":"It's bad enough having to clear out the wreckage of the racers without having to pick them out of burnt animal parts.","done":"I hope you didn't kill any of the basilisks on the tracks themselves! It takes a long time for the carcasses to decay in the sun, and I'd rather not have to take a shovel out to clean up.","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":81.6,"y":78,"n":"Trackmaster Zherin","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"375":{"id":375,"t":"The Chill of Death","lv":8,"min":7,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring five Duskbat Pelts and some Coarse Thread to Gretchen Dedmar in Brill.\n5 Duskbat Pelt Greater Duskbat 33 % , Vampiric Duskbat 33 %\nCoarse Thread sold by Tharynn Bouden , sold by Amy Davenport , sold by Gina MacGregor , sold by Gunder Thornbush and 4 more","desc":"It's so cold, now. The Plague of Undeath crawls through my veins like an icy serpent. The Mindless State will be upon me soon. But no doomed destiny will prevent me from serving our Dark Lady. When the call arose I sewed body bags for the fallen soldiers of Sylvanas's mighty army.\nNow my hands shake from the chill. If you would bring me five Duskbat Pelts and some Coarse Thread I could sew myself a blanket. Help me, ‹name›, so that I can continue to serve the cause.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nAdept's Cloak Sewing Gloves\nMoney: 2 25 0 gold, 2 silver, 25 copper Experience: 700\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Do you have five Duskbat Pelts and some Coarse Thread yet, ‹name›?","done":"I appreciate your efforts, ‹name›. May Slyvanas recognize your bravery one day. . . .","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.9,"y":52.7,"n":"Gretchen Dedmar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"3095":{"id":3095,"t":"Simple Scroll","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Read the Simple Scroll and speak to Dannal Stern in Deathknell.\nSimple Scroll\nProvided: Simple Scroll","desc":"Ah, while you were off dealing with the mindless Scourge, this scroll arrived for you. I would think it's some matter of importance as it seems it bears the seal of the warrior trainer Dannal. I would take some time to read it before heading out again.","rew":"Experience: 40\n+50 reputation with Undercity","back":"Ah, so you've arrived. Good. I overheard that a few others were able to escape \"death\" and were heading into town. Perhaps that resilence will pay off in the future also.\nYou may thank Sylvanas for your freedom... freedom of mind and body. Though you still remain tortured by the plague and its effects, you are now free to come and go as you see fit.","done":"I will be here to train you as you grow in experience... find me as often as you like. I charge a minimal fee, but you'll find everything I can teach you to be worthwhile.\nGo now and test your skill. Many more things will become known to you as you gain experience, some of which I am unable to discuss with you here. Just know that Sylvanas will need warriors with your type of strength in the future. You will be the backbone of our salvation. Do not forget it.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":30.8,"y":66.2,"n":"Shadow Priest Sarvis","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":32.7,"y":65.6,"n":"Dannal Stern","e":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"8295":{"id":8295,"t":"Quell the Silverwing Usurpers","lv":15,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 1,050 experience instead of 10,500, 0.1 times as much.","obj":"Enter Warsong Gulch and defeat the Alliance, gain a Warsong Gulch Mark of Honor, and bring it to Captain Shatterskull at the Mor'shan Base Camp.\nWarsong Gulch Mark of Honor","desc":"The wilds of the Ashenvale forest will succumb to the might of the Horde, ‹race›. Nothing the Silverwing say or do can stop our sovereign imperative. Kalimdor belongs to the Horde. How dare they attempt to prevent us from harvesting what is rightfully ours!\nLet the pride swell in your chest as you cut down their weak attempts at slowing our progress. Destroy the Silverwing Sentinels, and earn a Warsong mark of honor. Return to me with such a mark, ‹name›, and you will be rewarded.","rew":"Money: 20 0 gold, 20 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,050\n+200 reputation with Warsong Outriders\n+200 reputation with Warsong Outriders\n+200 reputation with Warsong Outriders\n+200 reputation with Warsong Outriders\nLevel 15 , requires level 10 Difficulty 10 11 13 18 22 Side Orc, Undead, Tauren, Troll Type PvP Shareable No Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8295","cats":["warsong-gulch"]},"5095":{"id":5095,"t":"A Call to Arms: The Plaguelands!","lv":50,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Seek out High Executor Derrington. His base camp is located at the Bulwark, east of Tirisfal Glades and the Undercity.","desc":"Heroes of the realm, hear me - the Horde calls upon you for swift action!\nA call to arms has been issued for all able bodied individuals to take up arms against the Scourge! Rumors fly of new threats rising from the ruins of the Eastern Kingdoms. They loom to the east of the Undercity, in the northern reaches of the lands now known as the Plaguelands!\nHeroes of the realm - seek out High Executor Derrington, who has set up his base camp at the Bulwark, east of Tirisfal Glades!","rew":"Experience: 470\n+10 reputation with Undercity","done":"Welcome to the Plaguelands, hero. This is one of the most dangerous frontiers in Azeroth, with the looming threat of the Scourge to our east, and then even further still eastward from there. I am glad to hear that the call of duty and service to the Horde did not fall on deaf ears with you!\nIf you are ready to get your hands dirty, then there is plenty for willing and able heroes to do here on the edge of the Plaguelands.\nThunder Bluff Tirisfal Glades","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":44.3,"y":58.8,"n":"Bluff Runner Windstrider","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":83.1,"y":68.9,"n":"High Executor Derrington","e":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"135":{"id":135,"t":"The Defias Brotherhood","lv":18,"min":14,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take Wiley's Note to Mathias Shaw in Stormwind.\nWiley's Note\nProvided: Wiley's Note","desc":"I wonder what Wiley meant when he mentioned the Stonemasons. Perhaps that was a slip of tongue. Could the Defias gang be related to the Stonemasons? Only one man would know for sure: Mathias Shaw, head of SI:7. Show him Wiley's Note and see if he has anything to add to this growing mystery. If you have trouble finding Shaw, check the Barracks in Old Town.","rew":"Experience: 675\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","back":"What business do you have with me? I am a very busy man. . .","done":"This matter might be more complex than Stoutmantle realizes.\nWestfall Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":56.3,"y":47.5,"n":"Gryan Stoutmantle","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":78.3,"y":70.7,"n":"Master Mathias Shaw","e":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"455":{"id":455,"t":"The Algaz Gauntlet","lv":21,"min":19,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Traverse Dun Algaz.\nKill 8 Dragonmaw Scouts and 6 Dragonmaw Grunts.\nReport to Valstag Ironjaw in Menethil Harbor.\nDragonmaw Scout slain : 0/ 8\nDragonmaw Grunt slain : 0/ 6","desc":"Orcs of the Dragonmaw clan have a haven in the Wetlands. And now they have expanded into Dun Algaz! We can't let them keep their foothold here or Loch Modan will be cut off from Menethil Harbor, our port and stronghold in the Wetlands.\nBreak through Dun Algaz to the Wetlands beyond, and kill some orcs for good measure! Report to Valstag Ironjaw in Menethil Harbor.\nMenethil is through Dun Algaz, then north along the road, then west at the fork.\nWe're counting on you, ‹name›. Do not fail.","rew":"Money: 10 0 gold, 10 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,250\n+75 reputation with Ironforge","back":"You're coming from Loch Modan? How is the orc situation at Algaz Gate?","done":"Your report is full of bad news!\nI see the Dragonmaws are making a strong move into Algaz. Normally the Dragonmaws just hide up in the hills. What made them surge into Algaz is still a mystery...\nThank you, ‹name›. And we'll probably want your help dealing with these orcs.\nLoch Modan Wetlands","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":25.4,"y":10.4,"n":"Mountaineer Rockgar","s":1},{"z":"Wetlands","x":10.1,"y":56.9,"n":"Valstag Ironjaw","e":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"295":{"id":295,"t":"Ormer's Revenge","lv":27,"min":22,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Ormer Ironbraid wants you to kill 10 Mottled Scytheclaw raptors and 10 Mottled Razormaw raptors then return to him at the Whelgar Excavation Site.\nMottled Scytheclaw slain : 0/ 10\nMottled Razormaw slain : 0/ 10","desc":"Now it's time to really make those dreaded Raptors regret their blood-thirst. Just down below there are scores of Mottled Scytheclaws and Mottled Razormaws. Make those rotten creatures pay by slaying 10 of each!","rew":"Money: 22 0 gold, 22 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,200\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"I want to make those Mottled Scytheclaws and Mottled Razormaws pay for what they did. Have you killed 10 of each yet?","done":"You did a bang-up job of clearing out those Raptors, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":38.2,"y":50.9,"n":"Ormer Ironbraid","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"93735":{"id":93735,"t":"The broken construct","lv":9,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Find Riaani Nightwind on the west side of Valanaar.","desc":"Historically, the Windshapers have seen to the tending of the magical instruments and devices that were gifted to us by the spirits of the wind. This includes the myriad of magical constructs around the island. Since the spirits left us, only a scant few of these are still functional.\nOne of the few remaining working constructs in Valanaar has become damaged. One of our artisans was dispatched to help, but he may be in need of aid. Travel to the west end of the city and offer any assistance you can.","done":"<Riaani's face is buried under the heaving armor plates of the construct, attempting to work on the mechanisms underneath. He does not notice your presence at all.>\nStorms curse where is the core?! Who thought it would be a good idea to remove the Gyrozephyr as well? It's a miracle this construct's winds haven't dissipated entirely by now!","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":59,"y":79.6,"n":"Ayessa Dawnsinger","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":59,"y":73,"n":"Riaani Nightwind","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]}});